# Build outputs and installs at ANY depth, not just the root: `COPY
# packages/backend/` would otherwise carry a local `packages/backend/dist` into
# the builder, where `tsc` emits over it without deleting stale files, and the
# runtime stage copies the whole of `dist/`. CI checks out none of these; a
# local build from a working tree has all of them.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.expo
.git
.worktrees/
packages/backend/uploads/
.github
*.md
infrastructure/
package-lock.json
**/coverage/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.claude/

# Never send local secrets or platform credentials to a Docker builder. No
# `.env` file is sent, the examples included: the build reads none of them, and
# a local copy of an example is the file most likely to be filled in by hand.
**/.env*
**/.npmrc
**/.aws/
**/.ssh/
**/credentials/
**/*credentials*.json
**/*service-account*.json
**/google-services.json
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p8
**/*.p12
**/*.jks
**/*.keystore

# The backend image never contains the client or SDK workspaces. Keep only the
# manifests needed to validate the full workspace lockfile — Bun's workspace
# filters exclude their dependency graphs, and the runtime stage deletes the
# directories outright.
packages/reviewer/*
!packages/reviewer/package.json
packages/console/*
!packages/console/package.json
packages/core/*
!packages/core/package.json

# Local-only planning notes. Untracked, so .gitignore does not keep them out of
# a build context.
.plan/
